+# Feature Specification: Coupon returned on cancel, free shipping at €50.00
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-09
+**Input**: (1) customer cancelled an order with a single-use welcome code; reorder refused "already used";
+(2) support: €4.90 shipping charged on goods of exactly €50.00.
+
+## Report 1 - Cancelling gives back a single-use coupon (fix)
+README "Orders"/"Discounts": cancelling gives back the coupon if single-use; it can be used again.
+Cause: `OrderService.cancel` released the coupon with the customer name; `place` records the order id.
+Boundaries: only the order that used the coupon can release it; cancelled order on day 14 still releases.
+
+## Report 2 - Free shipping from exactly €50.00 (already fixed, regression test added)
+README "Shipping": free when goods come to €50.00 or more, after discounts, before VAT.
+Code at HEAD already uses `>=` (fixed in 001). Order-level test added for goods of exactly 5000 cents,
+including goods reaching 5000 only after a discount (gross above) and 4999 still paying shipping.
+No code change needed; if the customer's order predates the 001 fix, it is not a current defect.
